{"name":"Crispa","hex":"#e7dfc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Ulmus 'Crispa'","blocks":[{"text":"The elm cultivar Ulmus 'Crispa' [:'curled', the leaf margin], sometimes known as the Fernleaf Elm, arose before 1800 and was first listed by Willdenow as U. crispa (1809). Audibert listed a U. campestris Linn. 'Crispa', orme à feuilles crépues [:'frizzy-leaved elm'], in 1817, and an Ulmus urticaefolia [:'nettle-leaved elm'] in 1832; the latter is usually taken to be a synonym. Loudon considered the tree a variety of U. montana (1838). In the 19th century, Ulmus × hollandica cultivars, as well as those of Wych Elm, were often grouped under Ulmus montana. Elwes and Henry (1913) listed 'Crispa' as a form of wych elm, but made no mention of the non-wych samara."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Ulmus_%27Crispa%27%2C_Serafimerparken%2C_Stockholm.jpg/330px-Ulmus_%27Crispa%27%2C_Serafimerparken%2C_Stockholm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulmus_'Crispa'","wikidata":"Q7879452"},{"title":"Crispa (clothing brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Crispa is a Philippine brand of shirts."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crispa_(clothing_brand)","wikidata":"Q110010542"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg/120px-Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg/250px-Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg/120px-Ulmus_glabra_Crispa_%28glabra%29_071007b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par